reason: Scanner.Scan dispatches only the default split (nil = ScanLines) via its __-helper; any non-nil SplitFunc — a custom function or an explicitly passed builtin (ScanWords here) — panics at Scan time because frontend/v1 cannot call through a 3-result function value held in a struct field (WS D)
retest: frontend/v1 supports multi-result function-value calls (WS D); then Scan dispatches s.split and this program passes
